Operation
ROS 2 controllers generate commands.
The hardware-interface plugins convert commands into the agreed embedded message format.
Each ESP32 validates and executes commands locally.
The ESP32s return feedback and fault/status data.
The hardware interfaces expose relevant state and command interfaces to ros2_control.
Advantages
Explicit control over message format and firmware behavior.
No micro-ROS Agent is required.
Clear separation between high-level ROS 2 logic and embedded control.
Can be developed and tested incrementally.
Disadvantages
must design and maintain the communication protocol.
