Advantages
May be suitable for a multi-controller system with specific wiring or electrical requirements.
CAN/CAN-FD can provide bus-level arbitration and error detection.
RS-485 supports differential signalling and can be appropriate for suitable multi-device serial networks.
Disadvantages
Requires compatible hardware and appropriate transceivers.
A communication protocol and ROS 2 driver are still needed.
Bus selection must account for bandwidth, timing, topology, cable length and electrical constraints.
Neither CAN nor RS-485 automatically provides ROS 2 topics or controller integration.
